From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:25:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 086/113] Loops: the DFA-filtered regvar synchronisation also
 covers register globals

A global variable of the main program is a register variable when no other
routine uses it; its loads are DFA-tracked like those of locals. Leaving it
out of get_used_live_regvars kept every such scalar live through the whole
loop, so mandelbrot's program-level doubles were spilled at every use again
(they had been register-allocated with the first version of the filter).
---
 compiler/ncgutil.pas | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler/ncgutil.pas b/compiler/ncgutil.pas
index 9eddc76b..8142f1d1 100644
--- a/compiler/ncgutil.pas
+++ b/compiler/ncgutil.pas
@@ -1185,9 +1185,14 @@ implementation
         vs: tabstractnormalvarsym;
       begin
         result:=false;
-        if not(sym.typ in [localvarsym,paravarsym]) then
+        if not(sym.typ in [localvarsym,paravarsym,staticvarsym]) then
           exit;
         vs:=tabstractnormalvarsym(sym);
+        { a global is a register variable only in the main program body when
+          no other routine uses it (and nothing takes its address) }
+        if (vs.typ=staticvarsym) and
+           not(vs.localloc.loc in [LOC_CREGISTER,LOC_CMMREGISTER,LOC_CFPUREGISTER]) then
+          exit;
         if (vs.typ=paravarsym) and
            paramanager.push_addr_param(vs.varspez,vs.vardef,current_procinfo.procdef.proccalloption) then
           exit;
